    "tutor": {
      "brief": "Six loads, fourteen kilos, three landings in order. The three critical loads weigh eleven together, so the grain only sails if something else does not. Ask where each thing should land, not just whether it goes. The pin matters here: what they choose to protect changes how far the boat gets.",
      "prompts": {
        "plan": [
          "Why that landing and not the next one?",
          "What happens if this never arrives?"
        ],
        "commit": [
          "What are you protecting above everything else?"
        ],
        "perturb": [
          "Which part of the plan just died?"
        ],
        "react": [
          "What is stranded now?"
        ],
        "revise": [
          "What goes back ashore to make this work?"
        ],
        "resolve": [
          "Was the grain worth the risk you took?"
        ]
      }
    },
